{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"258","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Little Elephant and Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant loves trees very much, he especially loves root trees."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He's got a tree consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" nodes (the nodes are numbered from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), with root at node number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each node of the tree contains some list of numbers which initially is empty. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant wants to apply "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations. On the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th operation "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ i ≤ m)"},{"kind":"text","text":" he first adds number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" to lists of all nodes of a subtree with the root in node number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":", and then he adds number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" to lists of all nodes of the subtree with root in node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After applying all operations the Little Elephant wants to count for each node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ j ≤ n; j ≠ i)"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that the lists of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th and the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th nodes contain at least one common number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the Little Elephant, count numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" for him."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n, m ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of the tree nodes and the number of operations. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two space-separated integers, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ui"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ui, vi ≤ n, ui ≠ vi)"},{"kind":"text","text":", that mean that there is an edge between nodes number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ui"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two space-separated integers, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ n, ai ≠ bi)"},{"kind":"text","text":", that stand for the indexes of the nodes in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the given graph is an undirected tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated integers — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c1, c2, ..., cn"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 1\n1 2\n1 3\n3 5\n3 4\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 3 3 3 3 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"11 3\n1 2\n2 3\n2 4\n1 5\n5 6\n5 7\n5 8\n6 9\n8 10\n8 11\n2 9\n3 6\n2 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 6 7 6 0 2 0 5 4 5 5 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"258E","schema"